    "icon": "data:image/png;base64,",
    "description": "Applies a regular expression to a text field: parse capture groups into fields, replace with back-references, tokenise matches into columns or rows, or flag matches.",
    "category": "Preparation",
    "subcategory": "Parse",
    "tags": [
        "regex",
        "regular expression",
        "parse",
        "extract",
        "tokenise",
        "replace",
        "visokio-agents"
    ],
    "introductoryText": "Regular expressions on a text field, with four modes:\n\n- **Parse**: each capture group `( )` becomes a new field. Named groups such as `(?P<Order>...)` name the fields; otherwise list names in *Output field names*\n- **Replace**: replace every match; use `\\1` or `$1` to insert captured text (for example, mask card numbers but keep the last four digits)\n- **Tokenise**: every match (or its first group) becomes a new **column** (up to a maximum) or a new **row**, such as all SKUs mentioned in a note\n- **Match**: a Yes / No field saying whether the text matches the pattern **anywhere**, **at the start** or **completely** (validation)\n\nCase can be ignored; text that is missing stays missing. Python regular expression syntax. Omniscope formulas can already search and replace with regular expressions; this block adds capture groups into fields, tokenising into rows, and a Yes / No match mode.",
